ng Services\nA\nResearch & Discovery\nResearch at LSU New Orleans\nStudent Research\nStudy Abroad\nInternational Center\nFaculty & Staff Research\nCollaborate with LSU New Orleans\nOffice of Research\nA\nAcademic Resources\nCourse Catalog\nRegistrar Office\nAcademic Calendar\nAbout\nA\nAbout Us\nMission & Vision\nHistory\nAt a Glance\nCurrent Rankings\nLooking for UNO?\nA\nLeadership & Offices\nOffice of the President\nAdministrative Offices\nUniversity Advancement\nWork at LSU New Orleans\nNews\nA\nCommunity & Engagement\nAlumni\nFor Parents\nService Learning\nMake a Gift\nA\nPolicies & Safety\nTitle IX\nCampus Safety\nNon Discriminatory Policy\nAccessibility\nA\nUniversity Resources\nContact LSU New Orleans\nCampus Map\nAlumni\nMake a Gift\nFor Faculty & Staff\nPrivateer Athletics\nExplore the shop and see upcoming games.\nStudent Life\nA\nStudent Life\nResidential Life\nApply for Housing\nDining Services\nHousing Rates\nPontchartrain Halls\nLafitte Village\nCampus Recreation\nA\nGet Involved\nStudent Organizations\nStudent Involvement & Leadership\nGreek Life\nFirst Year Experience\nService Learning\nSocial Media\nInternational Center\nA\nHealth & Wellness\nCampus Health Services\nTitle IX Resources\nStudent Accountability\nA\nCareer & Success\nCareer Services\nStudent & Alumni Resources\nResearch Opportunities\nStudy Abroad\nAcademic Advising\nGraduation Information\nA\nStudent Resources\nCampus Map\nTranscript Request\nThe Dock\nPrivateer Athletics\nExplore the shop and see upcoming games.\nAthletics\nvisit\nvisit\nvisit\napply\napply\napply\nSearch\nvisit\nvisit\nvisit\napply\napply\napply\nEdit Page\nLSU New Orleans\nacademics\ncollege of sciences\nmathematics\ngraduate programs\nhow to apply\nIN THIS SECTION\nGraduate Programs\nMathematics (M.S.)\nHow to Apply\nVisit Us\nApply to LSU New Orleans\nHow to Apply\nAdmission Requirements\nApplicants to the MS and PhD program must meet the following requirements for admission:\nOverall GPA requirement set by the graduate school: undergraduate 2.5, graduate 3.0.\nMathematics background: must have taken Math 2134 (Calculus III) and 3511 (Introduction to Linear Algebra) or equivalent.\nInternational applicants must satisfy the language requirement set by the graduate school.\nMS applicants meeting the above requirements are generally admitted to the program.\nTeaching assistant positions, which include a tuition waiver and a stipend, are competitive and all applications for TA positions are reviewed by the Graduate Advisory Committee. If available, submission of General GRE exam scores is encouraged for applicants interested in a TA position, though it is not required. Applicants interested in being considered for a TA position should notify Graduate Coordinator Linxiong Li.\nGraduate Coordinator\nLinxiong Li [email protected]\nSubmit an Application\nApplication is considered to be completed only if all required materials such as application fee payment and official transcripts are received by the deadline.\nPlease read the graduate checklist prior to completing the online application.\nGo to apply.uno.edu\nGo to the \"Graduate\" column and click on the the link\nClick the \"Create Account\" tab located on the top right-hand side of the page\nFill out the online application and attach the necessary documents\n*Please contact the Graduate Coordinator for list of necessary documents for the application.\nDetails about Graduate School admission requirements\nSubmit official transcripts from each institution that you have attended. International students may also need to submit certified English translations and evaluations of your transcripts. Learn more\nAfter your application packet is reviewed, you will receive an email with your LSU New Orleans student number.\nFooter\nContact\n2000 Lakeshore Drive New Orleans, LA 70148\n[email protected]\n[email protected]\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (504) 384-7924\n+1 (504) 384-7924\nLearn\nAdmission information\nPrograms of st